SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  No unit-suffixed field is read raw. The only SI-bearing value the page draws is the geofence radius (metres on the
  wire); it is handed verbatim to the SI-native Google Maps `Circle(radius = geofence.radius /* metres */)`, which
  consumes metres directly — no conversion, no non-SI storage. Guard config/events are ids/enums/timestamps (not unit
  bearing). Coordinates are WGS-84 degrees. Timestamps are formatted at the render boundary only (formatGuardTimestamp).

LIVE DATA / STALENESS (ADR-013)
  The web page treats vehicle state as a polled live source (useVehicleState refetchInterval 5 s armed / 30 s idle);
  there is no SSE source on this page. The Android port reproduces the poll via a viewModelScope ticker that bumps a
  lifecycle-aware (WhileSubscribed) re-fetch, and surfaces freshness honestly with a DataFreshness chip in the page
  header AND the Live-Map panel header bound to the vehicle-state feed's fetchedAt / refreshing / stale / error — so a
  reading older than its TTL (incl. the >2 min offline case) is shown as stale + retry rather than presented as live.

EVENT-LABEL / SENSITIVITY i18n (web hardcoded EVENT_LABELS + SENSITIVITY_OPTIONS)
  The web hardcodes the event-type display labels (emoji + name) and the sensitivity option labels as in-file
  constants. To honour the "zero hardcoded literals" rule rather than transplant English literals, both were lifted
  into res/values/strings.xml as extra translation_guard_event* / translation_guard_sensitivity* keys and resolved by
  the stable token (guardEventLabel / sensitivityLabel), keeping the web lookup-with-fallback (an unmapped event token
  renders verbatim — web `EVENT_LABELS[t] ?? t`). These extra keys have no web i18n counterpart (the web has none);
  the 38 manifest-required keys are unaffected.

